;; M7 named fallback: a recursive NON-SELECTIVE lattice (set union).
;; Distinct contributor rows can preserve the join -- deleting edge(5,2)
;; kills (2,{5}) while the cycle-derived (2,{1,5}) sustains the value, so
;; the value-unchanged skip cannot ground foundedness (the vetting probe
;; that found this hid an unfounded 2<->3 pair behind an unchanged join).
;; Non-selective heads report (reason lattice-nonselective-recount) and
;; the recursive repair refuses them: clear-and-rerun stays the exact
;; backstop until per-element contributor identity lands (7A.2).
lattice (iset (set int))
table (src int)
table (edge int int)
table (reach int iset)
rule (src S) (= R (cins (cmap) S)) --> (reach S R)
rule (reach X R) (edge X Y) --> (reach Y R)
